## Generators
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryofluid_synthesizer=Combines Titanium, Lapis Lazuli, and Water to produce Cryofluid. Stable mode uses 1 Titanium, 1 Lapis, and 1,000 mB Water to make 1,000 mB Cryofluid for 6,000 DE. Impulse mode uses 4 Titanium, 2 Lapis, and 4,000 mB Water to make 4,000 mB Cryofluid for 18,000 DE; Speed upgrades do not accelerate this profile.\n\nUse the orange button to switch profiles. Titanium and Raw Titanium are both accepted. Process Batch completes multiple conversions when enough items, Water, and tank space are available.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Titanium Input§r exposes the four Titanium slots.\n§bLapis Input§r exposes the four Lapis slots.\n§9Input All§r exposes all eight item inputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input§r fills the Water tank.\n§cCryofluid Output§r drains the Cryofluid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Titanium Input\n§r- §bLapis Input\n§r- §9Input All
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input\n§r- §cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_stabilizer=Consumes Cryofluid to turn supported unstable materials into their stabilized forms. Each input resolves directly to one indexed recipe, with its own processing time, energy cost, and Cryofluid cost.\n\nPlace filled Cryofluid Capsules in the capsule input; empty capsules leave through the adjacent return slot. Cryofluid can also enter directly through liquid I/O. The frozen input/output outlines, Cryofluid icon, and guide indicator show the dedicated stabilization path.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Material Input§r accepts unstable materials.\n§bCapsule Input§r accepts Cryofluid Capsules.\n§9Input All§r exposes both inputs.\n§cStabilized Output§r exposes recipe results.\n§cCapsule Return§r exposes empty capsules.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Cryofluid Input§r fills the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Material Input\n§r- §bCapsule Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cStabilized Output\n§r- §cCapsule Return\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Cryofluid Input
tile.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=Cryofluid Synthesizer\n§9Superior Cryo Synthesis Branch\n§7- Accepted upgrades:\n  §a§r, §b§r\n§o§9@UC: Ascendant Technology
entity.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=§fCryofluid Synthesizer
ui.utilitycraft:info.vaporworks_processor=Converts liquid inputs into pressurized Steam gas. Water produces Steam at a 1:1 ratio; Cryofluid takes longer and produces 50% more Steam. The liquid input tank and Steam gas tank each store 64,000 units.\n\nFilled Water or Cryofluid containers go in the upper-left slot and their empty containers leave below it. Empty gas capsules go in the upper-right slot; a filled 8,000-unit Steam Capsule leaves below it.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Liquid Container Input§r and §bGas Container Input§r accept containers.\n§cContainer Return§r and §cSteam Container Output§r expose processed containers.\n§9Input All§r and §cOutput All§r expose both pairs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Liquid Input§r accepts Water or Cryofluid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§cSteam Output§r exposes the Steam tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Container Input\n§r- §bGas Container Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cContainer Return\n§r- §cSteam Container Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cSteam Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.energizer=Converts supported iron materials into energized components. Place materials in either input; the Primary channel is checked first, then Auxiliary. Each recipe defines its own processing time and total energy cost.\n\nBoth channels resolve recipes through direct indexed lookup. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing, while Process Batch controls how many items complete per paid cycle.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Primary Input§r exposes the first-priority channel.\n§bAuxiliary Input§r exposes the fallback channel.\n§9Input All§r exposes both inputs.\n§cOutput§r exposes the result slot.
ui.utilitycraft:io.energizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Primary Input\n§r- §bAuxiliary Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.catalyst_weaver=Combines one base item with an exact set of up to six catalysts. Catalyst positions do not matter, but extra catalyst types prevent a match. Some recipes also consume Lava, Liquified Aetherium, or Dark Matter from the internal 128,000 mB tank.\n\nCatalyst Weaver recipes and registered UtilityCraft Infuser recipes are indexed when loaded. Recipe lookup does not scan the complete registry while machines run.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Base Input§r exposes the base item.\n§bCatalyst 1§r, §1Catalyst 2§r, §bCatalyst 3§r, §9Catalyst 4§r, §bCatalyst 5§r, and §1Catalyst 6§r each expose one catalyst slot.\n§3Input All§r exposes every item input.\n§cMain Output§r and §cResidue Output§r expose their respective results.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Catalyst Fluid Input§r exposes the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Base Input\n§r- §bCatalyst 1\n§r- §1Catalyst 2\n§r- §bCatalyst 3\n§r- §9Catalyst 4\n§r- §bCatalyst 5\n§r- §1Catalyst 6\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cMain Output\n§r- §cResidue Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Catalyst Fluid Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.liquifier=Converts supported solid materials into Liquified Aetherium or Dark Matter. Insert the solid material on the left; produced liquid accumulates in the output tank on the right. Some recipes can also create an optional solid residue.\n\nThe tank accepts one liquid type at a time and stores up to 640,000 mB. Drain it before switching between Liquified Aetherium and Dark Matter. The liquid can be extracted through liquid I/O or standard UtilityCraft fluid containers.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the solid material input.\n§cResidue Output§r exposes the optional byproduct.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cLiquid Output§r exposes the produced liquid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cResidue Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cLiquid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.residue_processor=Recovers useful materials from residue and other recyclable inputs. Place one supported material in the input slot; the primary result is stored in the upper output, while an optional chance-based residue is stored in the lower output.\n\nEvery input resolves directly to one recipe. Processing speed depends on recipe energy cost, installed upgrades, and the current process batch.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the material input.\n§cPrimary Output§r exposes the guaranteed result.\n§cResidue Output§r exposes the optional byproduct.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.
ui.utilitycraft:io.residue_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cPrimary Output\n§r- §cResidue Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:info.centrifugal_siever=Processes UtilityCraft sieve recipes through a shared four-slot input pool and a reusable Mesh. Drops are rolled once per processed item and stored in the 15-slot output buffer.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted cycle consumes 125 units per processed item, runs at 150% rate, and costs 125% energy.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes all material inputs.\n§bMesh§r exposes the mesh slot.\n§cOutput§r exposes the output buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §bMesh\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.dual_siever=Runs two UtilityCraft sieve lanes against one shared 20-slot output buffer. Each lane has one material input and its own reusable Mesh.\n\nIND mode charges both lane progress bars independently. SHR mode processes every ready lane through one coordinated progress bar at 72% rate and 135% combined energy cost.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted lane consumes 125 units per processed item, runs faster, and costs 125% energy.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Lane A Input§r / §bLane A Mesh§r.\n§9Lane B Input§r / §bLane B Mesh§r.\n§9All Inputs§r and §bAll Meshes§r expose both lanes.\n§cOutput§r exposes the shared buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Lane A Input\n§r- §bLane A Mesh\n§r- §9Lane B Input\n§r- §bLane B Mesh\n§r- §9All Inputs\n§r- §bAll Meshes\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.impact_crusher=Processes two Crusher recipes in parallel.\n\nEach lane has one input and a paired two-slot output buffer. Every craft consumes 400 mB of Lava.\n\nWater or Cryofluid can cool the machine. Cryofluid is more efficient, while passive cooling continues when idle.\n\nAt maximum heat, half of every input and output stack is destroyed and Thermal Lock activates. Cool the machine to 0 and change its inputs to restart it.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input 1§r and §cOutput 1§r use lane 1.\n§bInput 2§r and §cOutput 2§r use lane 2.\n§9Input All§r and §cOutput 3§r expose both lanes.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.\n§bCoolant Input§r accepts Water or Cryofluid.
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vFuel Input\n§r- §bCoolant Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.industrial_burner=Processes three Furnace recipes in parallel.\n\nEach lane has one input, one progress bar, and one output. Lava can add up to one bonus craft per base craft, consuming 250 mB for each bonus craft.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input 1§r and §cOutput 1§r use lane 1.\n§bInput 2§r and §cOutput 2§r use lane 2.\n§9Input 3§r and §cOutput 3§r use lane 3.\n§9Input All§r and §cOutput All§r expose all lanes.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §9Input 3\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vFuel Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.arc_press_forge=Processes Electro Press recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers. All four input slots form one pool, and all four output slots form another.\n\nUse the button below the progress bar to change modes. Low Loss preserves every output and charges progress at twice the base rate. High Speed doubles the process batch, but each completed batch has a 50% chance to lose one output.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.
ui.utilitycraft:io.arc_press_forge.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.pulverizer=Processes Crusher recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers. All four input slots form one pool, and all four output slots form another.\n\nThe machine runs normally without Steam. When Steam is available, each craft consumes 250 units, processing rate increases to 175%, and energy cost increases to 150%.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.pulverizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.pulverizer.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
